],
"notes":[
"A new Armory. Filters with icons down the left (All, Attack, Ability, Defense, Speed, Utility and a new Consumables tab for potions and scrolls; LB / RB switch them on a controller) and a search box. Items sit in sections by tier (Basic, Advanced, Legendary, Mythic) as bigger tiles with the price on a gold chip: green when the parts you own make it cheaper, red when you can't pay, a tick on what you own.",
"The details card shows the cost (with what your items cover), short stat lines, the unique and active, and the recipe as a small tree: parts, the item, what it builds into. Every icon is clickable (right-click buys).",
"The Buy button says why you can't buy (walk to the Armory, gold still needed, slots full). A status chip says whether you are at the Armory. Your six items and the potion sit along the bottom (right-click sells).",
"At big UI scales the Armory uses a compact layout: icon filters in the title row, your items above Buy."
]
}